# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BRS — .gitignore
# Written BEFORE `git init` on purpose. The archive is ~2 GB of
# images; a stray `git add .` without this file would be painful
# to undo. Do not remove the archive block.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── The archive (Plane 1 source material, ~2 GB) ──────────────
# These live in place for now. See docs/adr/0003-asset-source.md
# for the recommended move into assets-source/.
/BRS/
/BRS ExCom/
/BRS 11th ExCom Post/
/logo/
/mars-rover-frame/
/assets-source/

# Never commit raw or non-web source files
*.ai
*.eps
*.ARW
*.arw
*.heic
*.HEIC
*.psd
*.lnk

# ── Node ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Next.js ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.next/
out/
next-env.d.ts

# ── Turborepo ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.turbo/

# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
build/
.wrangler/

# ── Env & secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Graph credentials, Directus tokens, DB URLs. §12.2 — secrets
# live in the secret store, never in the repo.
.env
.env.*
# Templates must survive the rule above. `!.env.example` alone matched
# only that exact filename, so .env.production.example — the production
# handover document — was silently ignored and would never have been
# committed. The glob covers every future template too.
!.env*.example

# ── Test & audit artefacts ────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/
lighthouse-report*
.audit/

# ── Editor / OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
*.swp

# ── Database dumps ────────────────────────────────────────────
# pg_dump output taken before migrations. These carry live table
# contents — admin rows, hashes, tokens. Keep them local.
backup-before-*.sql.gz
*.sql.gz
*.dump
